WEBVTT

1
00:00:40.697 --> 00:00:43.116
<i>Peace.</i>

2
00:00:43.216 --> 00:00:45.517
<i>Long ago.</i>

3
00:00:45.518 --> 00:00:48.776
<i>before the founders established
this great city of ours</i>

4
00:00:48.977 --> 00:00:53.983
<i>that word was all but meaningless.
an ideal as elusive as a dream.</i>

5
00:00:54.618 --> 00:00:57.032
<i>Now. 200 years later.</i>

6
00:00:57.799 --> 00:01:01.961
<i>We are all of us living proof
that peace is indeed attainable.</i>

7
00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:05.918
<i>The reason for this is of
course are faction system.</i>

8
00:01:06.408 --> 00:01:11.058
<i>Erudite. Dauntless.
Amity. Candor. Abnegation.</i>

9
00:01:11.412 --> 00:01:14.796
<i>In dividing people according
to personality and attitude</i>

10
00:01:15.012 --> 00:01:19.224
<i>we've created a society in which
each faction plays a critical role</i>

11
00:01:19.425 --> 00:01:20.782
<i>in maintaining the social order.</i>

12
00:01:20.982 --> 00:01:24.371
<i>But this harmony we achieved
is now under attack from</i>

13
00:01:24.396 --> 00:01:27.721
<i>a small but extremely dangerous
group of individuals.</i>

14
00:01:27.897 --> 00:01:30.834
<i>We call them "Divergents".</i>

15
00:01:31.034 --> 00:01:35.165
<i>They are in essence the worst
of what humanity used to be</i>

16
00:01:35.657 --> 00:01:39.382
<i>rebellious. defiant. and uncontrollable.</i>

17
00:01:40.154 --> 00:01:43.590
<i>Five days ago. a rogue
group of divergents</i>

18
00:01:43.615 --> 00:01:47.345
<i>posing as Dauntless brutely
invaded Abnegation</i>

19
00:01:47.346 --> 00:01:49.247
<i>in an obvious attempt
to cripple the faction</i>

20
00:01:49.272 --> 00:01:51.382
<i>system by attacking it's
most vulnerable members.</i>

21
00:01:53.596 --> 00:01:58.790
<i>These divergents despise our system because
they are incapable of conforming to it.</i>

22
00:01:58.791 --> 00:02:02.661
<i>These latest rumours for example that I was
somehow behind the attack on abnegation</i>

23
00:02:02.875 --> 00:02:06.590
<i>is nothing more that divergent propaganda.</i>

24
00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:11.564
<i>I have devoted myself to bringing
these fugitives to justice.</i>

25
00:02:12.159 --> 00:02:15.331
<i>I've exercised my right as acting
council leader to declare martial law</i>

26
00:02:15.531 --> 00:02:20.217
<i>until im confident that any threat
to our security has been eliminated.</i>

27
00:02:20.687 --> 00:02:22.610
<i>Tell Jeanine we got it.</i>

28
00:02:24.793 --> 00:02:27.713
<i>We are all that's left of humanity.</i>

29
00:02:27.913 --> 00:02:29.536
<i>The vast wall that encloses this city</i>

30
00:02:29.736 --> 00:02:33.670
<i>may protect us from our toxic surroundings.</i>

31
00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:38.157
<i>but it is up to us to confront any element
that can poison us from within.</i>

32
00:02:38.357 --> 00:02:43.410
<i>Because when you are civilizations
last hope peace is not merely an ideal</i>

33
00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:45.667
<i>its an obligation.</i>

34
00:02:45.867 --> 00:02:50.423
<i>And it is up to all us to take a stand
position against it's one true enemy.</i>

35
00:02:51.665 --> 00:02:53.072
<i>Divergents.</i>

36
00:03:25.817 --> 00:03:28.164
Amity!

37
00:03:29.119 --> 00:03:31.186
We should make sure it's clear.

38
00:03:32.318 --> 00:03:33.662
Tris!

39
00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:53.459
Help us. help us. please!

40
00:03:55.188 --> 00:03:57.840
Please help us.
you have to help us!

41
00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:00.693
I'm sorry. you have to leave.

42
00:04:00.965 --> 00:04:04.382
- You just don't belong here.
- It's all her fault.

43
00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:12.015
You killed Will.

44
00:04:12.939 --> 00:04:14.121
No...

45
00:04:14.838 --> 00:04:15.989
She killed...

46
00:04:25.467 --> 00:04:26.582
Mom!

47
00:04:30.481 --> 00:04:33.617
You've killed us all.

48
00:06:26.890 --> 00:06:30.530
- And... Three!
- Higher!

49
00:06:32.916 --> 00:06:36.370
Higher. higher!
- Are you alright?

50
00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:38.587
Okay everyone back to you classroom

51
00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:55.413
I just wanted to do something different.

52
00:06:56.954 --> 00:06:58.300
Yeah.

53
00:07:10.833 --> 00:07:12.515
Well that's definitely different.

54
00:07:13.905 --> 00:07:18.093
- You dont like it?
- No. I like it. I like it alot

55
00:07:19.077 --> 00:07:20.897
I'm just surprised. that's all.

56
00:07:23.245 --> 00:07:26.850
- What's going on. Tris?
- Nothing. I'm fine.

57
00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:28.782
Just...

58
00:07:30.666 --> 00:07:32.331
Still having nightmares?

59
00:07:34.825 --> 00:07:36.044
No.

60
00:07:41.425 --> 00:07:43.257
We're good.

61
00:07:45.112 --> 00:07:49.412
You and me. I know nothing
else is. but we are.

62
00:07:56.048 --> 00:07:57.578
Time for chores.

63
00:08:13.308 --> 00:08:15.476
How much longer do we
have to stay here. Four?

64
00:08:15.501 --> 00:08:17.160
Until we know it's
safe to leave.

65
00:08:47.485 --> 00:08:50.306
- Hey.
- Hey.

66
00:08:51.058 --> 00:08:52.424
Son!

67
00:08:55.345 --> 00:08:57.252
You can't ignore me forever.

68
00:08:59.229 --> 00:09:02.793
I know you're thinking about your next
move. but there are things you don't know.

69
00:09:02.993 --> 00:09:04.933
Marcus. please just leave us alone.

70
00:09:06.628 --> 00:09:09.493
Your mother didn't come back to
abnegation just to save you.

71
00:09:09.693 --> 00:09:11.493
She died trying to hide
something from Jeanine

72
00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:12.996
that something entrusted
to Abnegation

73
00:09:13.172 --> 00:09:14.783
- long time ago.
- Marcus! Stop!

74
00:09:14.983 --> 00:09:17.453
Whatever you want from us.
you're not gonna get it.

75
00:09:21.444 --> 00:09:23.492
I'm not the enemy here.

76
00:09:36.078 --> 00:09:37.890
You found it...

77
00:09:41.079 --> 00:09:44.540
It was in the home of Natalie
and Andrew Prior. like you said.

78
00:09:52.214 --> 00:09:54.177
Want to tell me what's inside?

79
00:09:54.797 --> 00:09:58.891
A message from the founders that will
ensure the future of people who deserve it.

80
00:10:02.058 --> 00:10:08.568
Divergents will destroy our society.
unless we destroy them.

81
00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:15.014
And now we can.

82
00:10:15.897 --> 00:10:19.320
However. only a divergent
can open this box.

83
00:10:24.570 --> 00:10:26.033
Find them!

84
00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:28.798
Every last one of them.

85
00:10:47.442 --> 00:10:49.648
Go with happiness.

86
00:10:50.036 --> 00:10:51.831
Go with happiness.

87
00:10:52.404 --> 00:10:54.746
- You with happiness.
- Thank you.

88
00:10:58.948 --> 00:11:00.646
Go with happiness.

89
00:11:02.326 --> 00:11:05.400
I really don't know how much longer I
can do this whole peace and love thing.

90
00:11:05.871 --> 00:11:07.952
It's the amity way. just try to blend in.

91
00:11:08.532 --> 00:11:10.111
I'm trying to blend in.

92
00:11:10.136 --> 00:11:11.920
and its just not working.

93
00:11:12.241 --> 00:11:14.620
- Coming through. on you right.
Hey here we go.

94
00:11:14.621 --> 00:11:17.047
Look a rainbow. It's pretty.

95
00:11:18.312 --> 00:11:21.659
Pathological offendiness along without
questioning passivity. I love this place.

96
00:11:21.859 --> 00:11:24.125
Thank you. Go with happiness.

97
00:11:24.325 --> 00:11:27.794
- Oops. Excuse me.
- Hey tris. I really like your hair by the way.

98
00:11:27.995 --> 00:11:29.756
Did you try to cut it
all short and weird...

99
00:11:29.956 --> 00:11:32.461
Hey Peter. why don't you take
your food and sit down huh?

100
00:11:32.661 --> 00:11:33.823
Or what?

101
00:11:35.733 --> 00:11:38.973
Besides I think we all should stick together
now that we are officially fugitives.

102
00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:41.586
Wait what do you mean
by official fugitives?

103
00:11:41.611 --> 00:11:43.903
You don't know? You
did'nt tell Caleb?

104
00:11:44.173 --> 00:11:47.086
Yesterday Jeanine announced that
the attack on Abnegation

105
00:11:47.286 --> 00:11:51.067
was organized by a group of
regenade divergents And their sympathizers.

106
00:11:51.267 --> 00:11:52.863
So they're blaming
this whole thing on us?

107
00:11:52.888 --> 00:11:53.419
Yeah.

108
00:11:53.887 --> 00:11:55.722
And Jeanine needed a
reason to petition to the

109
00:11:55.747 --> 00:11:57.503
council so they could
institute martial law.

110
00:11:57.679 --> 00:11:59.495
And now she had one.

111
00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:09.921
Staying here at Amity is

112
00:12:09.946 --> 00:12:11.248
the best option for now.

113
00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.578
We need to keep an eye
of the ground and find

114
00:12:13.603 --> 00:12:15.163
out where the rest of
the dauntless are.

115
00:12:15.777 --> 00:12:19.513
- Then we can make a move.
- We need to kill Jeanine.

116
00:12:21.621 --> 00:12:24.097
I know. we're not ready yet.

117
00:12:29.265 --> 00:12:32.717
- Beatrice you're not being serious. right?
- No I am being serious..

118
00:12:33.717 --> 00:12:36.019
I'm not gonna stop until she's dead.

119
00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:38.661
Tris you can't just go
around killing people.

120
00:12:38.686 --> 00:12:40.332
She's right. listen
to your sister.

121
00:12:40.508 --> 00:12:42.170
Tris. I think you should go to

122
00:12:42.195 --> 00:12:44.132
erudite and kill
Jeanine yourself.

123
00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:45.717
I will stay with Caleb so

124
00:12:45.742 --> 00:12:46.907
they don't kill him too.

125
00:12:50.554 --> 00:12:51.682
What?

126
00:12:52.853 --> 00:12:54.279
C'mon you know.

127
00:12:55.473 --> 00:12:57.080
What you did with your parents.

128
00:13:13.922 --> 00:13:15.224
Stop!!!

129
00:13:15.424 --> 00:13:17.566
What do you think you're doing?

130
00:13:20.425 --> 00:13:22.907
- My office! Now!

131
00:13:24.863 --> 00:13:27.842
Enjoy your meal everyone. enjoy your meal.

132
00:13:28.042 --> 00:13:30.260
Hey. you need to calm down.

133
00:13:36.594 --> 00:13:41.455
Was I not clear that the terms of your
sanctuary here included non violence?

134
00:13:42.001 --> 00:13:44.947
Well I can guarantee you nothing
like this will ever happen again.

135
00:13:46.303 --> 00:13:49.992
Be that as it may. you can
no longer stay here with us.

136
00:13:50.192 --> 00:13:53.119
Your presence. it is just too disruptive.

137
00:13:55.709 --> 00:13:59.723
The truth is that our sanctuary was never
gonna last very long here anyways.

138
00:13:59.923 --> 00:14:02.989
Was it?
With you not standing up to Jeanine.

139
00:14:04.922 --> 00:14:07.848
- You don't understand us at all.
- No I do understand you.

140
00:14:08.049 --> 00:14:10.775
I understand that you think you can
stay out of this but you can't.

141
00:14:10.975 --> 00:14:13.261
One day she's gonna show up
and Jeanine is gonna take

142
00:14:13.286 --> 00:14:15.359
whatever power you think
you have away from you.

143
00:14:15.535 --> 00:14:16.536
Tris! Tris!

144
00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:23.091
Look. Johanna. we need a little more time.

145
00:14:23.942 --> 00:14:26.981
We need to find out where the rest of
the Dauntless are. then we can leave.

146
00:14:27.181 --> 00:14:29.639
And then what? Attack Erudite?

147
00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:33.403
- I will not be a part of your violence.
- No one is asking you to.

148
00:14:33.603 --> 00:14:36.491
We just need a few more days.

149
00:14:40.482 --> 00:14:42.171
One.

150
00:14:43.686 --> 00:14:48.516
- One. what?
- One more chance.

151
00:14:51.457 --> 00:14:57.065
See. to be Amity is to forgive
others. and yourself.

152
00:14:57.971 --> 00:15:00.188
You're hurting Tris.

153
00:15:03.151 --> 00:15:06.131
And my heart goes out to you.

154
00:15:07.675 --> 00:15:13.487
I know what it's like to stand helpless
while you loose the ones you love.

155
00:15:15.679 --> 00:15:18.596
But killing Jeanine will not
gonna bring your mother back.

156
00:15:19.615 --> 00:15:23.791
I know you're angry. but
you're letting it consume you.

157
00:15:26.705 --> 00:15:28.669
- What is it?

158
00:15:46.678 --> 00:15:48.951
Stay here and keep quite.

159
00:16:09.118 --> 00:16:13.000
Gentlemen. Amity welcomes you.

160
00:16:13.350 --> 00:16:16.667
- To what do we owe the pleasure.
- This isn't really a social call Johanna.

161
00:16:16.867 --> 00:16:19.993
- We're looking for divergents.
- I see.

162
00:16:20.193 --> 00:16:22.033
Well of course. anything
we can do to help.

163
00:16:22.058 --> 00:16:24.356
We need you to volunteer
your faction to be tested.

164
00:16:25.969 --> 00:16:28.577
This is screening technology from Erudite.

165
00:16:28.578 --> 00:16:29.886
Amity.

166
00:16:29.887 --> 00:16:31.378
Not that Jeanine is heading
up yo the council the

167
00:16:31.403 --> 00:16:32.803
whole improval processing
got a little easier.

168
00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:36.119
- You're exceeding your jurisdiction.
- Now. Johanna.

169
00:16:36.332 --> 00:16:39.210
What happened to that Amity politeness.

170
00:16:39.411 --> 00:16:45.292
The easy way. or the hard way?
It's up to you.

171
00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:53.227
Alright. but under protest.

172
00:16:54.416 --> 00:16:57.210
Okay we're good to go!
Move it out!

173
00:16:59.304 --> 00:17:03.812
All Amity report to the dome all come to
the dome for new mandatory testing.

174
00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:14.003
Ok. lets go. get inside!

175
00:17:27.775 --> 00:17:29.582
You know something lady?

176
00:17:31.028 --> 00:17:33.510
You seem awfully stuck in that doorway.

177
00:17:45.862 --> 00:17:49.305
Eric is here. We need to move now. come on.

178
00:17:57.434 --> 00:18:00.985
- What's up there?
- Just my office.

179
00:18:23.742 --> 00:18:25.088
There's two guards with guns.

180
00:18:26.654 --> 00:18:28.315
We're going out the window?

181
00:18:29.602 --> 00:18:31.303
We need to split up.

182
00:18:32.364 --> 00:18:35.573
Okey. yeah.

183
00:18:36.118 --> 00:18:37.896
Every man for hmself.

184
00:18:38.110 --> 00:18:39.491
Good.

185
00:18:41.007 --> 00:18:43.307
Hey. they're up here!

186
00:18:44.505 --> 00:18:46.872
Hey. they're up here! Come
qon they're getting away!

187
00:18:49.094 --> 00:18:50.506
You're ready?

188
00:19:03.753 --> 00:19:05.311
- Where?
- Out the window!

189
00:19:07.882 --> 00:19:09.692
I got three on foot
heading towards the dome!

190
00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:14.629
- Get them low!
- Repeat. three on foot toward the dome.

191
00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:16.100
Over there!

192
00:19:16.301 --> 00:19:18.324
- I demand amnisty!
- Sit down! Sit down!

193
00:19:18.524 --> 00:19:20.548
I believe in Abignation. it's my right!

194
00:19:28.805 --> 00:19:31.911
- Detain him!
- Let's go!

195
00:19:39.937 --> 00:19:41.641
Come on. keep moving!

196
00:19:52.783 --> 00:19:53.897
Run!

197
00:19:54.559 --> 00:19:55.712
Run!

198
00:20:03.668 --> 00:20:05.421
Come on!

199
00:20:40.060 --> 00:20:42.237
- Listen!
- What?

200
00:20:42.437 --> 00:20:43.702
A train!

201
00:20:45.584 --> 00:20:46.764
Go. go. go!

202
00:20:52.344 --> 00:20:53.515
Caleb!

203
00:20:54.546 --> 00:20:55.548
Keep moving.

204
00:21:04.785 --> 00:21:06.030
Ammo!

205
00:21:20.684 --> 00:21:21.930
Come on. go.

206
00:21:42.438 --> 00:21:44.044
- Go. go!
- Caleb!

207
00:21:45.274 --> 00:21:46.357
Move!

208
00:22:22.535 --> 00:22:24.480
You sure know how to make an entrance!

209
00:22:29.634 --> 00:22:33.104
- Factionless.
- Amity.

210
00:22:33.386 --> 00:22:35.773
Oh. you stare like dogs.

211
00:22:37.359 --> 00:22:39.203
I have no idea what this one is.

212
00:22:39.403 --> 00:22:43.431
- Look. we just need to get to the city. thats all.
- Well to bad. the train is taken.

213
00:22:43.745 --> 00:22:46.738
And you damaged our cargo.

214
00:22:49.651 --> 00:22:54.020
These are Abnegation and
you are factionless right?

215
00:22:54.220 --> 00:22:55.681
- Caleb!
- I used to be Abnegation.

216
00:22:55.881 --> 00:22:59.070
We used the same bolts
to make cloth for you.

217
00:23:00.821 --> 00:23:02.602
Are you saying that we steal from you?

218
00:23:03.433 --> 00:23:06.433
No no. I'm no longer Abnegation.
so technically you're not stealing from me.

219
00:23:06.458 --> 00:23:09.283
No. you're not stealing at all.

220
00:23:09.483 --> 00:23:14.367
It's a questions of semantics I suppose
wether it's stealing or sharing.

221
00:23:14.567 --> 00:23:16.447
- But it's all really the same.
- That's enough!

222
00:23:16.528 --> 00:23:18.797
Everybody relax alright.
You've made your point.

223
00:23:18.998 --> 00:23:22.366
- We'll get off your train alright.
- Guy. would everybody just relax?

224
00:23:22.566 --> 00:23:24.195
Why don't we take a seat?

225
00:23:27.677 --> 00:23:29.824
- I was just trying to help!
- Don't.

226
00:23:30.024 --> 00:23:31.357
Yeah. this is going to be fun.

227
00:23:31.557 --> 00:23:33.572
Everybody calm down alright?

228
00:24:53.514 --> 00:24:54.555
Caleb.

229
00:25:01.770 --> 00:25:03.937
Get off! Get off!

230
00:25:31.225 --> 00:25:32.494
- You alright?
- Yup.

231
00:25:32.694 --> 00:25:33.965
Are you okay?

232
00:25:45.332 --> 00:25:48.061
- Tobias Eaton.
- Say it again.

233
00:25:48.895 --> 00:25:50.660
Tobias Eaton.

234
00:25:52.989 --> 00:25:54.600
What you know him?

235
00:25:55.491 --> 00:25:56.642
I am him.

236
00:26:03.479 --> 00:26:05.463
We have been looking for you.

237
00:26:07.188 --> 00:26:08.788
What are they talking about? <br />Four!

238
00:26:26.895 --> 00:26:27.978
Follow me.

239
00:26:33.579 --> 00:26:36.421
Tris! I'm sorry. I wanted to help.

240
00:26:47.161 --> 00:26:51.016
Four! Four! Why are they looking for you?

241
00:26:51.983 --> 00:26:53.715
How do they know your your name?

242
00:27:06.420 --> 00:27:08.272
This is factionless.

243
00:27:09.960 --> 00:27:11.745
This is insane.

244
00:27:48.421 --> 00:27:49.633
Tobias!

245
00:27:53.517 --> 00:27:54.996
Mother.

246
00:28:02.100 --> 00:28:03.646
I thought she was dead.

247
00:28:07.094 --> 00:28:08.255
Me too.

248
00:28:24.909 --> 00:28:26.929
Somebody please tell me
what's going on here.

249
00:28:31.665 --> 00:28:34.272
Tobias's father was very abusive.

250
00:28:35.661 --> 00:28:39.377
I knew the only way I could
ever truly escape him was...

251
00:28:39.577 --> 00:28:41.289
to disappear completely.

252
00:28:43.706 --> 00:28:46.396
Abnegation helped me fake my death.

253
00:28:46.669 --> 00:28:49.223
Anything to protect Marcus image.

254
00:28:49.423 --> 00:28:52.111
But you just left him
there alone with Marcus.

255
00:28:53.062 --> 00:28:54.793
I was very young.

256
00:28:56.220 --> 00:28:58.492
I reached out to him about a year ago.

257
00:28:59.077 --> 00:29:01.594
I felt it was finally time to reconnect.

258
00:29:03.401 --> 00:29:06.760
- I'm still your mother.
- No. my mother is dead.

259
00:29:08.358 --> 00:29:10.532
I went to her funeral when I was six.

260
00:29:12.212 --> 00:29:14.850
And she wasn't trying to reconnect with me.

261
00:29:15.051 --> 00:29:17.690
She was trying to use me.
Like you are now.

262
00:29:17.890 --> 00:29:18.891
What?

263
00:29:20.192 --> 00:29:21.514
She wants an army.

264
00:29:22.212 --> 00:29:24.127
- An army?
- I want an alliance.

265
00:29:24.327 --> 00:29:27.216
- No. what you want is revenge!
- This isn't about me.

266
00:29:27.416 --> 00:29:29.466
It's about putting an
end to a system that

267
00:29:29.491 --> 00:29:31.731
says one group is more
deserving than another.

268
00:29:31.907 --> 00:29:36.164
This city may be surrounded by a wall
but it doesn't have to be a prison.

269
00:29:36.835 --> 00:29:38.414
I think that's a bit extreme.

270
00:29:38.896 --> 00:29:41.919
I mean. the factions isn't meant
to be perfect but it's hardly a prison.

271
00:29:42.119 --> 00:29:45.026
Let me guess. you're Erudite?

272
00:29:47.377 --> 00:29:48.556
I was Erudite.

273
00:29:53.607 --> 00:29:56.973
- Are you willing to kill Jeanine?
- Absolutely.

274
00:29:58.581 --> 00:30:00.753
When I was married to
Marcus I knew her well.

275
00:30:00.953 --> 00:30:03.280
And believe me. there's
nothing she isn't capable of.

276
00:30:03.480 --> 00:30:08.642
- But I think you already know that.
- Tris. we can't trust her.

277
00:30:09.565 --> 00:30:12.348
- Maybe she knows...
- We're on the same side. Tris.

278
00:30:13.548 --> 00:30:16.652
I'm factionless because I
don't fit in any one faction.

279
00:30:16.852 --> 00:30:19.957
And you're Divergent because
you belong to too many..

280
00:30:20.157 --> 00:30:22.713
But we are both a threat to Jeanine.

281
00:30:23.629 --> 00:30:26.464
My people are ready for war
if that's what it takes.

282
00:30:26.664 --> 00:30:27.665
And then what?

283
00:30:29.123 --> 00:30:32.286
- We depose those in power.
- And once you've done that?

284
00:30:33.618 --> 00:30:36.931
Once you killed Jeanine.
who's in power then?

285
00:30:37.951 --> 00:30:42.355
You see. that's the part she
always conveniently leaves out.

286
00:30:44.497 --> 00:30:47.867
Don't tell me this isn't about
you. this is only about you.

287
00:30:50.702 --> 00:30:53.637
I know where the remaining
Dauntless are hiding.

288
00:30:53.837 --> 00:30:56.795
- Where?
- They took shelter in Candor.

289
00:30:56.995 --> 00:30:58.477
As far as I know they're still there.

290
00:30:59.978 --> 00:31:02.354
Think about it. If we
were to combine forces.

291
00:31:02.554 --> 00:31:06.692
Dauntless and Factionless.
we'd be unstoppable.

292
00:31:06.892 --> 00:31:08.097
That's not gonna happen.

293
00:31:08.298 --> 00:31:12.908
Thank you for your hospitality.
but we will be leaving in the morning.

294
00:31:13.108 --> 00:31:14.363
Four. maybe this is...

295
00:31:14.563 --> 00:31:16.726
Tobias. please reconsider.

296
00:31:17.197 --> 00:31:18.813
Don't you call me that.

297
00:31:21.411 --> 00:31:22.840
My name is Four.

298
00:31:32.151 --> 00:31:34.424
You want to talk him in. or should I?

299
00:31:57.580 --> 00:31:59.253
The food looks lovely.

300
00:32:01.712 --> 00:32:03.002
Thank you.

301
00:32:16.498 --> 00:32:17.644
I'm sorry.

302
00:32:25.145 --> 00:32:27.221
I should've told you about her.

303
00:32:37.887 --> 00:32:39.896
No more secrets.

304
00:32:41.076 --> 00:32:42.482
Okay?

305
00:32:53.166 --> 00:32:56.263
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to wake you.

306
00:33:00.773 --> 00:33:03.298
I always loved to watch him sleep.

307
00:33:07.143 --> 00:33:09.851
I take it you're setting out
to Candor in the morning?

308
00:33:10.051 --> 00:33:11.052
Yeah.

309
00:33:16.377 --> 00:33:20.201
Listen. I only want what's best for him.

310
00:33:22.150 --> 00:33:23.972
You hardly even know him.

311
00:33:26.120 --> 00:33:28.337
You'd like to think
that wouldn't you?

312
00:33:28.362 --> 00:33:31.884
But deep inside I think you're
scared I know him all to well.

313
00:33:34.641 --> 00:33:36.930
- Im not scared.
- Of course you are.

314
00:33:37.130 --> 00:33:41.211
You're scared that he'll finally
see you for what you really are.

315
00:33:43.614 --> 00:33:45.490
Deadly.

316
00:33:48.393 --> 00:33:50.114
You don't believe me?

317
00:33:53.997 --> 00:33:55.691
Ask him.

318
00:34:02.318 --> 00:34:03.845
Are you okey?

319
00:34:04.045 --> 00:34:05.046
Yeah.

320
00:34:07.461 --> 00:34:10.057
- Sure?
- Yeah.

321
00:34:59.712 --> 00:35:02.795
- Im not going with you guys.
- What?

322
00:35:04.747 --> 00:35:07.977
To Candor. I'm not going with you guys.

323
00:35:11.710 --> 00:35:14.267
- What are you talking about?
- What's your plan?

324
00:35:15.941 --> 00:35:17.896
You guys are gonna find the rest
of the Dauntless and then what?

325
00:35:18.348 --> 00:35:19.526
You attack Erudite?

326
00:35:19.727 --> 00:35:22.371
Assasinate Jeanine and start a civil war?

327
00:35:23.347 --> 00:35:26.000
Im sorry. I'm just not cut out for that.

328
00:35:27.967 --> 00:35:29.520
I'm not like you guys.

329
00:35:33.664 --> 00:35:39.005
I need to get back to Abnegation maybe...
...Maybe I can be usefull there.

330
00:35:39.251 --> 00:35:42.159
Caleb. there's nothing left in Abnegation.

331
00:35:44.438 --> 00:35:45.558
Yeah.

332
00:36:18.987 --> 00:36:21.800
- You okey?
- We just need to get to Candor.

333
00:36:25.333 --> 00:36:26.374
Triss!

334
00:36:30.394 --> 00:36:34.735
I know you think Caleb is your
responsibility but he made his own choice.

335
00:36:35.799 --> 00:36:37.647
You can't protect everyone.

336
00:36:39.349 --> 00:36:43.099
- I can't protect anyone.
- Nobody can.

337
00:36:44.027 --> 00:36:48.231
Him leaving isn't your fault.
None of this is your fault.

338
00:36:50.363 --> 00:36:53.745
Johanna was right. You
have to forgive yourself.

339
00:37:01.294 --> 00:37:02.336
Thank you.

340
00:37:03.585 --> 00:37:05.342
We gotta move.

341
00:37:32.571 --> 00:37:34.678
- We found them!
- Yeah.

342
00:37:39.927 --> 00:37:41.828
- Damn it's good to see you guys.
- How are you?

343
00:37:42.028 --> 00:37:44.108
I'm better now. I'm not
exactly good for layong low.

344
00:37:44.129 --> 00:37:45.459
- Triss!
- Christina!

345
00:37:48.785 --> 00:37:51.010
- It's so good to see you.
- You too.

346
00:37:51.211 --> 00:37:53.246
Have you heard anything about Will?

347
00:37:56.520 --> 00:37:58.398
- No.
- Nothing?

348
00:37:58.598 --> 00:37:59.599
No.

349
00:38:00.991 --> 00:38:02.690
Something must have happened to him.

350
00:38:03.572 --> 00:38:05.491
He would've found me by now you know.

351
00:38:07.173 --> 00:38:09.404
- Hey.
- Hey.

352
00:38:10.241 --> 00:38:11.472
How are you holding up?

353
00:38:12.942 --> 00:38:15.246
- How many Dauntless do we have?
- 175 total.

354
00:38:15.446 --> 00:38:17.949
- 175? That's it?
- The rest followed Max.

355
00:38:18.149 --> 00:38:20.653
- Not nearly the number we need.

356
00:38:20.853 --> 00:38:23.585
Hold it! Grab the guns!

357
00:38:25.817 --> 00:38:28.546
- Hey. they're with us.
- We know who you are.

358
00:38:28.746 --> 00:38:31.476
Last warning. Drop your guns.

359
00:38:33.966 --> 00:38:35.376
Alright.

360
00:38:46.919 --> 00:38:48.337
Easy.

361
00:39:00.572 --> 00:39:04.114
- I'm Jack Kang. I'm leadership here.
- We know who you are.

362
00:39:04.314 --> 00:39:05.999
We are not a threat to Candor.

363
00:39:06.099 --> 00:39:08.984
That might be your truth.
it's not neccesarily mine.

364
00:39:09.851 --> 00:39:13.881
All I know for certain is you are both wanted
for criminal insurgency and conspiring

365
00:39:14.081 --> 00:39:15.641
in the attack on Abnegation.

366
00:39:19.369 --> 00:39:20.426
Those are lies.

367
00:39:20.526 --> 00:39:23.502
If you were Candor I would
take you at your word.

368
00:39:25.235 --> 00:39:28.475
Unfortunately given the circumstances I'm
obliged to hand you over to the council.

369
00:39:28.623 --> 00:39:31.706
- You can make your case there.
- You might as well kill us now.

370
00:39:31.906 --> 00:39:35.081
If Jeanine finds us. we're not
gonna live to stand trial.

371
00:39:35.281 --> 00:39:38.456
I doubt that very much.
She would never supersede the council.

372
00:39:38.656 --> 00:39:42.358
Are you sure about that?
Who's gonna stop her? You?

373
00:39:43.602 --> 00:39:45.834
Factional law must be upheld.

374
00:39:46.034 --> 00:39:47.948
No. wait wait wait.

375
00:39:48.416 --> 00:39:50.168
Can I ask you one question?

376
00:39:51.635 --> 00:39:53.096
Can I ask you one question?

377
00:39:53.296 --> 00:39:57.855
Jeanine believes that Erudite are the most
fit to govern because they are the smartest.

378
00:39:57.955 --> 00:40:01.362
You believe Candor is the most fittest
to judge because you are so honest?

379
00:40:01.562 --> 00:40:03.989
I admit. I hold that belief.

380
00:40:04.189 --> 00:40:06.763
Then. would you say I
trial held here at Candor

381
00:40:06.963 --> 00:40:09.538
would be inherently more fair
than a trial held by Erudite?

382
00:40:13.880 --> 00:40:15.522
The answer is yes.

383
00:40:15.722 --> 00:40:20.303
In my opinion a Candor trial would have the
greatest chance of achieving true justice.

384
00:40:20.786 --> 00:40:24.434
So you are asking me to petition a
council at the great Candor...?

385
00:40:24.635 --> 00:40:28.283
No. As part of Candors initation
you administer a truth serum.

386
00:40:28.483 --> 00:40:29.484
Correct.

387
00:40:31.546 --> 00:40:34.210
We dont technically discuss such
matters with other factions.

388
00:40:34.411 --> 00:40:37.076
- It's a pretty evasive answer.
- Evasion is not dishonest.

389
00:40:37.276 --> 00:40:38.682
But it's not exactly honest either.

390
00:40:40.214 --> 00:40:44.099
- Yes. we possess such a serum.
- Then use it on us.

391
00:40:44.300 --> 00:40:45.401
Four!

392
00:40:45.501 --> 00:40:48.103
If we are guilty. we
surrender to the council.

393
00:40:48.303 --> 00:40:51.097
If not. you just saved two lives.

394
00:40:51.297 --> 00:40:54.598
- And gain some loyal allies.
- Alright.

395
00:40:54.798 --> 00:40:57.130
But you should know the
serum can be quite brutal.

396
00:40:57.331 --> 00:41:01.736
It was designed for tender applicants who
are already predisposed to honesty.

397
00:41:01.936 --> 00:41:04.932
Not everyone find it so easy
to share their secrets.

398
00:41:06.593 --> 00:41:08.897
- I do not want to do it.
- We have to.

399
00:41:09.561 --> 00:41:12.017
Neither of us have secrets worth dying for.

400
00:41:22.052 --> 00:41:23.981
Let the truth set you free.

401
00:41:41.660 --> 00:41:42.711
Tobias Eaton.

402
00:41:46.735 --> 00:41:50.666
You are accused of conspiring with your
fellow Dauntless in the attack on Abnegation.

403
00:41:51.249 --> 00:41:53.006
Is this true?

404
00:41:54.882 --> 00:41:56.900
Conspiring no.

405
00:41:57.101 --> 00:41:58.918
But I did attack.

406
00:41:59.118 --> 00:42:01.619
I was in simulation
controlled by Jeanine and

407
00:42:01.644 --> 00:42:04.088
the rest of the Dauntless
she had recruited.

408
00:42:05.206 --> 00:42:06.688
Tris found me.

409
00:42:07.985 --> 00:42:13.321
She managed to break me free from the
simulation and together we fought are way out.

410
00:42:18.521 --> 00:42:21.545
So you are saying that Jeanine
orchestrated this attack?

411
00:42:23.114 --> 00:42:24.466
Yes.

412
00:42:28.984 --> 00:42:30.596
One last thing.

413
00:42:32.087 --> 00:42:36.861
If you suspected that Jeanine had corrupted
Dauntless. why didn't you just leave?

414
00:42:38.318 --> 00:42:40.466
Why did you stay?

415
00:42:40.875 --> 00:42:42.883
I wanted to leave.

416
00:42:43.958 --> 00:42:46.240
But I fell in love with Tris Prior.

417
00:42:49.713 --> 00:42:51.383
And I could not leave her.

418
00:43:00.012 --> 00:43:02.171
Thank you for your Candor.

419
00:43:02.371 --> 00:43:04.330
Thank you for your Candor.

420
00:43:04.530 --> 00:43:07.174
Tobias Eaton. this trial
has concluded and you are

421
00:43:07.199 --> 00:43:09.841
resolved of the guilt on
the attack on Abnegation.

422
00:43:12.394 --> 00:43:13.968
Miss Prior if you would.

423
00:43:25.286 --> 00:43:27.065
Let the truth set you free.

424
00:43:42.025 --> 00:43:43.291
Tris Prior.

425
00:43:45.513 --> 00:43:47.939
Mr Eaton said you managed
to free him from the sim.

426
00:43:50.599 --> 00:43:51.927
Yes.

427
00:43:52.360 --> 00:43:54.692
So you were never under
the simulation yourself.

428
00:43:56.015 --> 00:43:57.050
No.

429
00:43:58.176 --> 00:43:59.716
How is that possible?

430
00:44:01.124 --> 00:44:03.307
Because im divergent.

431
00:44:09.769 --> 00:44:11.433
I see.

432
00:44:14.180 --> 00:44:18.614
So you never harmed any of your fellow
Dauntless or the Abnegation?

433
00:44:18.815 --> 00:44:22.647
I did.

434
00:44:30.293 --> 00:44:31.431
Who?

435
00:44:34.397 --> 00:44:35.944
My mom.

436
00:44:38.433 --> 00:44:43.971
I watched her die first and then my dad.

437
00:44:44.071 --> 00:44:46.853
They were killed trying to save me.

438
00:44:54.608 --> 00:44:58.730
Miss Prior. the more you resist.
the more painfull the serum will be.

439
00:45:06.364 --> 00:45:10.995
My friend... I killed my friend.

440
00:45:11.713 --> 00:45:13.780
He was trying to shoot me.

441
00:45:20.972 --> 00:45:22.664
And... I shot him first.

442
00:45:26.837 --> 00:45:28.697
What was his name?

443
00:45:35.129 --> 00:45:36.977
What was his name?

444
00:45:40.716 --> 00:45:45.206
Will. I killed Will.

445
00:45:49.888 --> 00:45:57.854
This is what happens to
people that get close to me.

446
00:46:06.443 --> 00:46:07.985
They get hurt or they die.

447
00:46:10.686 --> 00:46:13.230
I can't forgive myself.

448
00:46:16.125 --> 00:46:18.201
Thank you for your Candor.

449
00:46:18.402 --> 00:46:20.477
Thank you for your Candor.

450
00:46:35.736 --> 00:46:38.851
Tris!

451
00:46:42.121 --> 00:46:44.060
Im sorry.

452
00:46:45.409 --> 00:46:47.884
I told you I didnt want to do that.

453
00:47:00.367 --> 00:47:01.368
- Christina.
- Go.

454
00:47:04.729 --> 00:47:06.056
Go.

455
00:47:15.335 --> 00:47:17.667
Abnegation sim complete.

456
00:47:19.340 --> 00:47:20.542
Dauntless sim initiated.

457
00:47:24.285 --> 00:47:26.512
Mam. the Divergents viable is dropping.

458
00:47:26.712 --> 00:47:29.295
If we dont pull her out of
the sim soon we'll loose her.

459
00:47:29.320 --> 00:47:30.497
You stop when I say so.

460
00:47:37.230 --> 00:47:38.918
She's gonna do it.

461
00:47:43.127 --> 00:47:45.056
She's gonna pass the sim.

462
00:47:48.199 --> 00:47:50.884
Dauntless sim failed.

463
00:47:52.251 --> 00:47:54.684
Divergent test subject
six is no longer viable.

464
00:47:57.836 --> 00:47:59.814
Alright shut it down.

465
00:48:02.150 --> 00:48:03.617
We are wasting our time.

466
00:48:05.693 --> 00:48:09.973
I've been asuming all the
Divergents are the same.

467
00:48:12.961 --> 00:48:15.460
But some are stronger than others.

468
00:48:17.822 --> 00:48:21.460
Assign all non essential
personnel to Divergent detail.

469
00:48:21.738 --> 00:48:23.663
We need to work harder.

470
00:48:24.130 --> 00:48:26.285
We need to find that very special one.

471
00:48:46.200 --> 00:48:48.151
Where's your scary boyfriend?

472
00:48:51.888 --> 00:48:54.131
Probably out doing scary boyfriend things.

473
00:49:00.029 --> 00:49:01.717
Mind if I join you?

474
00:49:06.466 --> 00:49:07.913
I love heights.

475
00:49:09.832 --> 00:49:12.174
Up here everyting seems
much smaller. you know.

476
00:49:14.927 --> 00:49:16.842
I know it sounds crazy. but...

477
00:49:17.209 --> 00:49:21.082
Sometimes I think I see
lights out beyond the wall.

478
00:49:23.244 --> 00:49:27.367
I know they say its all just
wasteland out there but...

479
00:49:29.212 --> 00:49:32.418
We can't be the only ones left. Can we?

480
00:49:37.795 --> 00:49:38.952
C'mon!

481
00:49:39.152 --> 00:49:41.310
- Got any weapons?
- No!

482
00:50:59.463 --> 00:51:01.081
Coast clear. moving out!

483
00:51:29.365 --> 00:51:32.480
Mommy! Mommy!

484
00:51:34.851 --> 00:51:39.402
That thing hurt me?

485
00:51:40.295 --> 00:51:42.286
You see? It's ok.

486
00:51:43.073 --> 00:51:47.544
It's just something to help you go to
sleep. I need you to do me a favour.

487
00:51:47.744 --> 00:51:49.954
You have to go to the
top of the stairs and

488
00:51:49.979 --> 00:51:52.239
don't come down until
your mommy comes here.

489
00:51:52.415 --> 00:51:55.560
Don't come down. Can you do that?

490
00:51:57.018 --> 00:51:58.526
Be brave. ok?

491
00:51:59.679 --> 00:52:01.993
Ok. go.

492
00:52:37.940 --> 00:52:39.121
Hey!

493
00:52:39.655 --> 00:52:41.325
Why are we the only ones awake?

494
00:52:42.637 --> 00:52:44.098
Because we're Divergents.

495
00:52:44.298 --> 00:52:46.918
Come on. I need your help to open this.

496
00:52:47.119 --> 00:52:48.999
I need your help.

497
00:52:54.603 --> 00:52:55.731
Hey!

498
00:52:56.292 --> 00:52:59.071
Look who decided to show up.

499
00:53:06.219 --> 00:53:08.177
It's really good to see you again.

500
00:53:14.327 --> 00:53:17.918
Alright folks. nothing to be nervous about.

501
00:53:18.600 --> 00:53:22.230
It's a little routine inspection.
then we all go back to our business.

502
00:53:24.751 --> 00:53:25.919
Hello.

503
00:53:30.602 --> 00:53:33.058
Divergent 10 %.

504
00:53:34.473 --> 00:53:35.869
Shit.

505
00:53:36.607 --> 00:53:38.220
You're almost normal.

506
00:53:39.219 --> 00:53:40.231
That's boring.

507
00:53:42.801 --> 00:53:44.452
That is not part of the mission.

508
00:53:44.652 --> 00:53:45.803
So what?

509
00:53:47.237 --> 00:53:49.597
As far as I'm concerned the
rest of them are still outlaws.

510
00:53:50.380 --> 00:53:54.251
Let's just wrap this up quick.
The others is gonna be awake soon.

511
00:54:06.648 --> 00:54:08.531
- Hi. sweetie.
- I should not...

512
00:54:11.349 --> 00:54:15.149
- Divergent 40%.
- I'm afraid it's not you either.

513
00:54:17.056 --> 00:54:18.553
The lady said that I should not...

514
00:54:19.426 --> 00:54:22.629
The lady said that I shouldn't
have come downstairs.

515
00:54:23.120 --> 00:54:25.077
Maybe you should have listened.

516
00:54:36.247 --> 00:54:39.034
Enough! You still have to test her.

517
00:54:41.603 --> 00:54:43.468
Jeanine stold us we have to test everyone.

518
00:54:51.043 --> 00:54:54.789
- Divergent 100%.
- I'll be damned.

519
00:54:55.090 --> 00:54:57.725
- What?
- She's what we've been looking for.

520
00:54:58.362 --> 00:55:00.300
Bullshit.

521
00:55:04.267 --> 00:55:06.706
Divergent 100%.

522
00:55:09.182 --> 00:55:10.373
Get her in the veichle.

523
00:55:10.733 --> 00:55:12.324
I'll alert Jeanine.

524
00:55:16.644 --> 00:55:19.788
If you think you got lucky. you are wrong.

525
00:55:20.799 --> 00:55:23.246
You gonna wish I killed you.

526
00:55:38.367 --> 00:55:40.150
Drop your weapons!

527
00:55:54.973 --> 00:55:56.174
Thank you.

528
00:55:58.027 --> 00:55:59.668
It's lucky you got that gun Four.

529
00:56:02.121 --> 00:56:05.037
We both know your'e not much without one.

530
00:56:36.283 --> 00:56:40.241
You think you're safe now?
You're wrong.

531
00:56:41.327 --> 00:56:43.387
Jeanine will never gonna
stop searching for you.

532
00:56:46.962 --> 00:56:52.551
Why? What she want with her? Tell me!

533
00:56:52.787 --> 00:56:57.523
It's exactly what Jeanine needs.
It's the perfect subject.

534
00:57:01.255 --> 00:57:03.225
Is that supposed to scare me?

535
00:57:04.946 --> 00:57:07.794
You're responsible for the
death of hundreds of people.

536
00:57:07.819 --> 00:57:09.547
You know the
punishment for that.

537
00:57:10.289 --> 00:57:14.960
Listen... I found a way to live
with the blood on my hands.

538
00:57:16.493 --> 00:57:17.720
But can you?

539
00:57:49.089 --> 00:57:50.700
Why dont they come out?

540
00:57:50.974 --> 00:57:53.916
All I know is that they put me sleeping
and then all hell break lose.

541
00:57:53.917 --> 00:57:55.117
Heck. don't play!

542
00:58:06.413 --> 00:58:07.790
You know what this means.

543
00:58:09.057 --> 00:58:10.418
Thank you.

544
00:58:10.989 --> 00:58:14.152
- For helping us.
- I wish I could do more.

545
00:58:15.173 --> 00:58:17.595
I had no idea Jeanine was capable
of something like this.

546
00:58:18.636 --> 00:58:21.008
It's time we fight back.

547
00:58:21.118 --> 00:58:22.769
- We don't have the numbers.
- We will.

548
00:58:24.625 --> 00:58:26.103
Once we get the Factionless.

549
00:58:30.973 --> 00:58:31.984
You heard Eric.

550
00:58:32.653 --> 00:58:37.043
Jeanine is not gonna stop coming after you.
It's are only option.

551
00:58:42.995 --> 00:58:47.044
Tris Prior. Of course.

552
00:58:47.045 --> 00:58:49.100
It had to be her.

553
00:58:49.975 --> 00:58:52.482
- Is she still off the grid?
- Yeah.

554
00:58:52.867 --> 00:58:54.970
But I think I found a solution.

555
00:58:58.883 --> 00:59:01.572
- It's Peter. right?
- Yeah.

556
00:59:02.156 --> 00:59:06.140
Jeanine. can I just say it's truly an honor
to finally meet you in person.

557
00:59:08.077 --> 00:59:09.255
Congratulations mother.

558
00:59:10.658 --> 00:59:11.912
You got your war.

559
00:59:12.425 --> 00:59:16.437
- I know you wish there was another way.
- But there isn't.

560
00:59:19.562 --> 00:59:21.793
I'm the lesser of two evils. is that it?

561
00:59:27.760 --> 00:59:30.642
- It better be.
- Tell me...

562
00:59:31.783 --> 00:59:33.619
Why did you surrender to Erudite?

563
00:59:35.577 --> 00:59:37.178
What do you want?

564
00:59:38.900 --> 00:59:41.472
I would like a position in your regime.

565
00:59:42.573 --> 00:59:46.103
Ideally I would like a position with
some advancement opportunities.

566
00:59:47.738 --> 00:59:49.742
I may be Dauntless but I'm
not just some meathead.

567
00:59:51.712 --> 00:59:53.564
No offense. Max.

568
00:59:57.737 --> 01:00:00.057
Prove your worth to us.

569
01:00:01.090 --> 01:00:03.065
Then we can discuss your ambitions.

570
01:00:03.432 --> 01:00:04.834
Great.

571
01:00:05.764 --> 01:00:07.106
When do I start?

572
01:00:07.136 --> 01:00:09.538
Let's talk about your friend Tris Prior.

573
01:00:11.370 --> 01:00:14.402
- How do I flush her out?
- It's simple.

574
01:00:14.403 --> 01:00:17.238
The girl is a walking bleeding heart.
She was borne out of Abegnation.

575
01:00:17.295 --> 01:00:19.897
It's her weak spot. You just
have to know how to press it.

576
01:00:20.468 --> 01:00:22.969
Help! Come quick.

577
01:00:33.146 --> 01:00:37.687
Traitor Tris Prior must be
surrendered to Erudite.

578
01:00:37.688 --> 01:00:40.231
Or every day more death will follow.

579
01:00:46.488 --> 01:00:47.582
Hand over Tris Prior.

580
01:00:48.919 --> 01:00:51.046
Or every day more death will follow.

581
01:00:53.939 --> 01:00:55.814
Hand over Tris Prior.

582
01:00:56.304 --> 01:00:58.845
Or every day more death will follow.

583
01:01:03.632 --> 01:01:05.041
Hand over Tris Prior.

584
01:01:05.241 --> 01:01:07.839
- Or every day more death will follow.
- Christina!

585
01:01:08.040 --> 01:01:09.041
No!

586
01:01:22.054 --> 01:01:23.496
Christina!

587
01:01:24.277 --> 01:01:25.608
Help me!

588
01:01:26.439 --> 01:01:27.570
Tris!

589
01:02:04.555 --> 01:02:06.761
We removed this from the
body of the suicidal.

590
01:02:07.056 --> 01:02:11.283
Marlene. Her name was Marlene.

591
01:02:11.899 --> 01:02:14.704
I'm sorry. Marlene.

592
01:02:15.692 --> 01:02:18.005
It's a very sophisticated
sim serum injector.

593
01:02:18.326 --> 01:02:20.148
It also has a radio
transmitter in it's head.

594
01:02:20.208 --> 01:02:23.466
- How do we get them out?
- I don't know.

595
01:02:23.611 --> 01:02:25.908
This tech was built to defend itself.

596
01:02:26.143 --> 01:02:27.294
This tendril...

597
01:02:28.315 --> 01:02:30.289
wraps around the nearest major artery.

598
01:02:30.317 --> 01:02:34.723
If you try to removed them...
and it kills the host.

599
01:02:35.262 --> 01:02:36.473
Kill the host?

600
01:02:39.225 --> 01:02:40.534
So what do we do?

601
01:02:40.535 --> 01:02:43.728
Tori must neutralize the disk
before we do anything else.

602
01:02:43.830 --> 01:02:45.777
Or we can do the logical thing.

603
01:02:46.222 --> 01:02:47.653
We hand her over.

604
01:02:47.963 --> 01:02:52.210
Nobody knows about this alliance.
we have to protect that advantage.

605
01:02:52.211 --> 01:02:53.869
If we hand Tris over now...

606
01:02:54.900 --> 01:02:57.401
it might buy some time.

607
01:03:05.811 --> 01:03:07.164
I think it's a good idea.

608
01:03:07.712 --> 01:03:10.478
But you have to go through me first.

609
01:03:10.779 --> 01:03:13.137
- Me too.
- And us.

610
01:03:25.882 --> 01:03:28.389
I am the one with a time bomb in my arm!

611
01:03:59.176 --> 01:04:01.041
I know what you're thinking.

612
01:04:03.885 --> 01:04:05.650
But I'm not gonna let you do it.

613
01:04:13.128 --> 01:04:15.350
I can't let anyone else die because of me.

614
01:04:15.688 --> 01:04:17.787
No one else is gonna die because of you.

615
01:04:18.247 --> 01:04:20.217
Tori will disable the disk.

616
01:04:20.417 --> 01:04:23.613
- And if she doesn't?
- Then...

617
01:04:26.056 --> 01:04:29.873
If she doesn't. we figure it out.

618
01:04:31.159 --> 01:04:32.262
Together.

619
01:04:33.323 --> 01:04:34.968
You know. I'm just one person.

620
01:04:38.220 --> 01:04:40.838
- I'm not worth it.
- You are worth it.

621
01:04:41.038 --> 01:04:42.990
You are more than worth it to me.

622
01:04:44.747 --> 01:04:46.428
I love you.

623
01:06:56.773 --> 01:07:00.288
This city may be safe behind a closed wall.

624
01:07:00.763 --> 01:07:05.459
but make no mistake. that wall alone
doesnt ensure our security.

625
01:07:07.457 --> 01:07:14.340
It's up to us. everyone of us. to remain
vigilant and isolate any threat against us.

626
01:07:15.593 --> 01:07:19.706
There are individuals hiding among
us who must be contained.

627
01:07:20.514 --> 01:07:24.386
Permit me to address the objections from
my fellow faction leaders.

628
01:07:25.451 --> 01:07:29.078
I'm aware that there has been some concerns
about the unavoidable raid on Candor

629
01:07:29.079 --> 01:07:32.632
so let me be clear.

630
01:07:34.185 --> 01:07:37.617
The harbouring of
Divergents from any faction

631
01:07:37.618 --> 01:07:39.527
can not be tolerated.

632
01:07:41.318 --> 01:07:44.150
Very soon I will present
what I believe to be no

633
01:07:44.175 --> 01:07:47.123
less than a mandates from
the founders themselves.

634
01:07:47.975 --> 01:07:53.270
On this I have no doubt on the measure
I have taken to keep the peace.

635
01:07:53.963 --> 01:07:58.427
I have provided instructions that will allow
us to eradicate the Divergence crisis.

636
01:07:58.428 --> 01:08:00.252
Once and for all.

637
01:08:15.417 --> 01:08:16.949
Where are you going?

638
01:08:17.815 --> 01:08:19.456
She has left. She's gone.

639
01:08:20.961 --> 01:08:23.252
What? When?

640
01:08:23.882 --> 01:08:25.461
- Last night.
- Wait.

641
01:08:29.627 --> 01:08:32.949
Tobias! People look to you for leadership.

642
01:08:33.060 --> 01:08:35.312
You can't just abandon them

643
01:08:40.223 --> 01:08:41.339
Tobias!

644
01:08:51.107 --> 01:08:52.158
Wow!

645
01:08:54.210 --> 01:08:56.269
I have to admit that I'm surprised.

646
01:08:57.597 --> 01:08:59.558
I mean. I know that you are dumb but..

647
01:08:59.895 --> 01:09:03.247
I didn't think you were dumb enough
to actually come down here.

648
01:09:03.448 --> 01:09:05.009
And turn yourself in.

649
01:09:10.783 --> 01:09:12.266
The killings had to stop.

650
01:09:13.338 --> 01:09:16.677
That just shows that you can
take the girl from Abnigation

651
01:09:16.911 --> 01:09:19.014
but you cant take Abnigation out of her.

652
01:09:19.583 --> 01:09:21.735
Let's go.

653
01:09:22.336 --> 01:09:24.837
Once a stiff. always a stiff. Right?

654
01:09:35.448 --> 01:09:39.271
- What is this?
- What is this? This is the whole reason you are locked Tris.

655
01:09:40.012 --> 01:09:43.075
Man I love knowing stuff you don't.

656
01:09:43.855 --> 01:09:46.037
I need you to open that box Tris.

657
01:09:51.913 --> 01:09:55.282
The only way to open that box is to
pass the sims of all five factions.

658
01:09:57.238 --> 01:10:00.473
But te only people who have
tried to it so far have died.

659
01:10:04.218 --> 01:10:06.058
I don't think I was
supposed to tell you that.

660
01:10:06.483 --> 01:10:07.591
Well...

661
01:10:08.618 --> 01:10:10.270
No pressure.

662
01:10:11.099 --> 01:10:12.441
Remarkable!

663
01:10:13.607 --> 01:10:17.962
The chances of it being you of all people.

664
01:10:18.817 --> 01:10:21.290
You're the... laws of probability.

665
01:10:24.866 --> 01:10:27.195
As remarkable as many people
you managed to murder?

666
01:10:29.938 --> 01:10:32.402
Dark times call for extrme measures.

667
01:10:34.562 --> 01:10:37.352
You may find it hard to believe.

668
01:10:37.422 --> 01:10:39.963
But I'm serving the greater good.

669
01:10:42.459 --> 01:10:44.151
Step up on the disc please.

670
01:11:05.661 --> 01:11:07.873
Step up on the disc please.

671
01:11:16.000 --> 01:11:17.181
Mam?

672
01:11:26.099 --> 01:11:28.851
Stop the suicides or I
swear I will shoot him.

673
01:11:29.392 --> 01:11:33.865
That's okey. You can kill him if you want.
we have plenty of guards.

674
01:11:35.435 --> 01:11:36.768
What?

675
01:12:14.823 --> 01:12:19.910
I'm guesing you need me alive
for this to work. Right?

676
01:12:22.591 --> 01:12:23.822
Right?!

677
01:12:36.899 --> 01:12:39.105
Tris.

678
01:12:42.119 --> 01:12:43.380
Caleb.

679
01:12:45.309 --> 01:12:46.683
Caleb.

680
01:12:47.004 --> 01:12:50.587
Don't engage to subject.

681
01:12:52.188 --> 01:12:53.828
Conditions are already less then optimal.

682
01:13:03.249 --> 01:13:04.350
My God.

683
01:13:15.179 --> 01:13:18.033
If I do this the suicides stop?

684
01:13:20.494 --> 01:13:24.149
No. The suicides will continue.

685
01:13:24.698 --> 01:13:28.149
Until you suced and pass all five sims.

686
01:13:29.503 --> 01:13:32.116
That should be sufficient enough.

687
01:13:34.938 --> 01:13:36.149
Good luck.

688
01:14:48.180 --> 01:14:49.301
Let's begin.

689
01:14:51.583 --> 01:14:53.549
Initialize the Dauntless sim.

690
01:15:13.355 --> 01:15:16.581
Mom.

691
01:15:19.551 --> 01:15:20.765
Tris. help me!

692
01:15:51.235 --> 01:15:53.046
Heart rate is rising.

693
01:15:54.578 --> 01:15:55.895
Keep her in play.

694
01:16:15.445 --> 01:16:16.636
Mom!

695
01:16:26.811 --> 01:16:28.513
I'm coming.

696
01:17:03.860 --> 01:17:05.827
Mom!

697
01:17:10.031 --> 01:17:11.533
I'm coming.

698
01:17:57.392 --> 01:17:58.765
Tris!

699
01:17:59.599 --> 01:18:01.157
Hold on!

700
01:18:11.996 --> 01:18:13.340
Tris.

701
01:18:15.181 --> 01:18:17.151
Dauntless sim complete.

702
01:18:31.664 --> 01:18:35.199
- I miss you so much.
- I know you do.

703
01:18:36.726 --> 01:18:38.393
But I'm still with you..

704
01:18:49.814 --> 01:18:51.568
You need to be strong now.

705
01:18:53.063 --> 01:18:54.824
Tell me you're gonna be strong.

706
01:18:55.370 --> 01:18:57.405
- I'm trying.
- You can do this.

707
01:18:57.730 --> 01:18:59.520
I know you can.

708
01:19:00.184 --> 01:19:04.382
You're brave. Braver than anyone.

709
01:19:05.867 --> 01:19:07.960
I'm not brave mom.

710
01:19:10.874 --> 01:19:13.192
I pretend that I am.

711
01:19:14.159 --> 01:19:17.031
I want people to think
that I am. but I'm not.

712
01:19:21.060 --> 01:19:23.867
I'm really really scared and...

713
01:19:24.529 --> 01:19:27.562
Maybe we are actually
what's wrong in this world.

714
01:19:29.196 --> 01:19:31.065
Divergents.

715
01:19:32.346 --> 01:19:35.080
I never wanted any of this.

716
01:19:35.949 --> 01:19:39.362
You and dad and Caleb and Four.

717
01:19:40.178 --> 01:19:46.720
I can't help but think that if I was normal
we would all still be together.

718
01:19:48.545 --> 01:19:51.489
Mom. I don't want to be Divergent anymore.

719
01:19:51.490 --> 01:19:54.678
I just want to feel safe again.

720
01:19:57.538 --> 01:19:59.814
Candor sim complete.

721
01:20:19.798 --> 01:20:22.571
Four. You're here?

722
01:20:22.771 --> 01:20:24.217
Yeah. I'm here.

723
01:20:26.302 --> 01:20:28.001
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

724
01:20:29.398 --> 01:20:30.910
Secure the hallway.

725
01:20:34.793 --> 01:20:36.160
Let's get you out of here.

726
01:20:38.060 --> 01:20:39.238
- You good?
- Yeah.

727
01:20:53.940 --> 01:20:55.809
Stop. Let him go.

728
01:20:56.590 --> 01:20:58.119
Wait. you're not gonna shoot me?

729
01:20:59.116 --> 01:21:00.911
Once a stiff. always a stiff.

730
01:21:13.694 --> 01:21:14.770
Go!

731
01:21:21.596 --> 01:21:24.828
Four. how did you get passed security?

732
01:21:24.829 --> 01:21:27.475
You know me. scary boyfriend skills.

733
01:21:32.220 --> 01:21:33.424
What is it?

734
01:21:36.453 --> 01:21:39.634
You weren't there. You
didn't even hear that.

735
01:21:41.626 --> 01:21:42.837
Tris.

736
01:21:43.376 --> 01:21:45.158
We need to leave now. Alright?

737
01:21:46.599 --> 01:21:48.134
I'm sorry Four.

738
01:21:48.918 --> 01:21:52.006
- What?
- I'm sorry I didn't tell you I was gonna go.

739
01:21:53.155 --> 01:21:54.533
I wanted to say goodbye.

740
01:21:54.559 --> 01:21:56.109
but I just didnt know how.

741
01:21:56.285 --> 01:21:59.157
- I didn't know how.
- What are you talking about?

742
01:22:03.114 --> 01:22:06.208
Even though I didn't
get to say it in

743
01:22:06.233 --> 01:22:09.571
real life. at least I
get to say it now.

744
01:22:09.984 --> 01:22:14.144
- Even if it is just a sim.
- Tris. we're not in a sim.

745
01:22:14.855 --> 01:22:18.734
Don't you think I would
know if I were in a sim?

746
01:22:18.759 --> 01:22:21.211
Four... you're not in a sim.

747
01:22:23.958 --> 01:22:27.649
- You're the sim.
- Wait. wait.

748
01:23:00.370 --> 01:23:02.249
Erudite sim complete.

749
01:23:03.109 --> 01:23:06.919
- There's only Amity now.
- She hasn't passed Abnegation yet.

750
01:23:06.920 --> 01:23:09.916
Yes she has. When she spared your life.

751
01:23:12.142 --> 01:23:14.349
This girl is extraordinary.

752
01:23:15.120 --> 01:23:16.430
She tested positive for

753
01:23:16.455 --> 01:23:17.933
four factions in one day.

754
01:23:20.482 --> 01:23:22.241
No one has gotten that far.

755
01:23:23.839 --> 01:23:25.050
We got a problem.

756
01:23:30.635 --> 01:23:32.863
She's crashing. We have to rest her.

757
01:23:33.948 --> 01:23:36.828
Are you sure you're not letting
familiar attachment cloud your judgement?

758
01:23:37.051 --> 01:23:38.399
See for yourself.

759
01:23:46.459 --> 01:23:47.520
Very well.

760
01:23:49.762 --> 01:23:51.350
Detach the subject.

761
01:24:02.664 --> 01:24:05.969
Good work. gentlemen. We
will resume tomorrow.

762
01:24:48.653 --> 01:24:51.766
You were never planing on going
back to Abnegation. were you?

763
01:24:54.635 --> 01:24:56.656
I had to do what I though was right.

764
01:24:57.567 --> 01:24:59.902
My parents would be ashamed of you.

765
01:25:01.235 --> 01:25:03.912
Well maybe not. I mean I'm

766
01:25:03.937 --> 01:25:06.614
willing to sacrifice you.

767
01:25:07.714 --> 01:25:09.320
The only family I have left.

768
01:25:09.420 --> 01:25:10.540
The only person that I love.

769
01:25:10.563 --> 01:25:12.675
In order to preserve what's
best for everyone else.

770
01:25:15.529 --> 01:25:17.191
What's more selfless than that?

771
01:25:25.987 --> 01:25:27.609
What does Jeanine think

772
01:25:27.634 --> 01:25:29.185
is in that box Caleb?

773
01:25:29.529 --> 01:25:31.104
It's a message from the founders.

774
01:25:31.608 --> 01:25:35.903
But the box was to be opened
only if the factions broke down.

775
01:25:35.904 --> 01:25:36.904
Which is why we require

776
01:25:36.928 --> 01:25:38.187
someone like you to open it.

777
01:25:39.444 --> 01:25:41.463
You're living proof
that the Divergent

778
01:25:41.488 --> 01:25:43.454
problem has grown
beyond all control.

779
01:25:44.177 --> 01:25:45.326
Do you even hear what you

780
01:25:45.351 --> 01:25:46.362
are saying right now?

781
01:25:47.591 --> 01:25:49.009
No one think it's your fault

782
01:25:49.034 --> 01:25:50.502
that you were born this way.

783
01:25:50.694 --> 01:25:52.954
Jeanine murdered an entire faction Caleb.

784
01:25:52.955 --> 01:25:55.204
That faction could no longer be trusted.

785
01:25:55.205 --> 01:25:56.490
She killed our parents.

786
01:25:56.491 --> 01:25:59.112
Are parents brought that on themselves.

787
01:25:59.312 --> 01:26:00.392
What are you talking about?

788
01:26:01.849 --> 01:26:04.106
The box. it was in their house.

789
01:26:04.107 --> 01:26:06.010
They were the ones hiding it.

790
01:26:06.011 --> 01:26:08.114
All those lives could have been spared.

791
01:26:10.150 --> 01:26:12.550
Seems we didnt knew our parents
as well as we thought we did.

792
01:26:15.436 --> 01:26:18.059
Alright family reunion is
over. it's time to go.

793
01:26:26.273 --> 01:26:28.627
I got a little surprise for you Tris.

794
01:26:32.608 --> 01:26:34.271
- Four!
- Tris!

795
01:26:34.579 --> 01:26:38.410
Tris!

796
01:26:38.610 --> 01:26:43.913
Four!

797
01:26:51.349 --> 01:26:56.750
I gather your brother explained how vital the work
you're doing here is to the future of the city.

798
01:26:56.950 --> 01:26:58.316
Please just let Four go.

799
01:26:59.897 --> 01:27:04.806
If his well being is such a concern you
should focus on the task at hand.

800
01:27:07.312 --> 01:27:10.005
Tell me...
Do you appreciate irony?

801
01:27:11.067 --> 01:27:15.675
You tested positive for Erudite so
you must have the intellectual capacity.

802
01:27:16.079 --> 01:27:17.177
Irony.

803
01:27:17.178 --> 01:27:19.301
For instance. Right
now you are full of

804
01:27:19.326 --> 01:27:21.501
hate. but you need to
pass an Amity sim.

805
01:27:26.555 --> 01:27:29.145
Then there are other ironies at work too.

806
01:27:29.504 --> 01:27:31.899
- Such as the fact your cherish mother...
- Don't.

807
01:27:31.900 --> 01:27:34.024
That you so dauntlessly
saved in the sim is

808
01:27:34.049 --> 01:27:36.244
the reason you're in
this mess to begin with.

809
01:27:36.245 --> 01:27:37.665
You're the reason I'm in this mess.

810
01:27:37.666 --> 01:27:39.946
- And then there the most
pointed irony of all.

811
01:27:39.971 --> 01:27:40.705
- Stop.

812
01:27:40.706 --> 01:27:45.310
That Nathalie Prior not only died trying
to protect the data that I now have.

813
01:27:45.311 --> 01:27:46.338
Because you stole them.

814
01:27:46.363 --> 01:27:47.365
You killed her for it!

815
01:27:47.366 --> 01:27:49.608
Data that she so selfishly

816
01:27:49.633 --> 01:27:52.366
withheld. But her own daughter.

817
01:27:52.367 --> 01:27:56.767
her beloved Divergent Tris is going to
be the one who delivered it to me.

818
01:27:56.768 --> 01:27:57.888
- I said stop!
- Therefore...

819
01:27:58.705 --> 01:28:02.566
your mother's death. just like
your boyfriend's death...

820
01:28:02.567 --> 01:28:05.422
will mean absolutely nothing.

821
01:29:13.623 --> 01:29:18.206
Don't pull her out. Not yet.

822
01:30:09.360 --> 01:30:11.383
No!

823
01:30:12.514 --> 01:30:13.719
Bring her back!

824
01:30:16.778 --> 01:30:18.119
Bring her back.

825
01:30:19.781 --> 01:30:21.122
Now!

826
01:30:22.019 --> 01:30:23.256
Bring her back!

827
01:30:23.456 --> 01:30:24.856
Come on!

828
01:30:25.056 --> 01:30:27.061
Come on!

829
01:30:30.773 --> 01:30:31.913
Bring her back!

830
01:30:32.042 --> 01:30:33.839
Test subject seven is no longer viable.

831
01:30:58.106 --> 01:31:00.142
I really thought you were the one.

832
01:31:12.516 --> 01:31:13.617
We just...

833
01:31:16.553 --> 01:31:20.296
We just have to resume are search.

834
01:31:35.118 --> 01:31:37.618
Find solace in your faction. Caleb.

835
01:31:38.011 --> 01:31:39.921
We are your family now.

836
01:32:26.695 --> 01:32:28.397
Jeanine wanted me to show you this.

837
01:32:58.146 --> 01:33:00.489
Hey. Four. can you do that thing you do?

838
01:33:07.244 --> 01:33:09.116
Hey Four. that's pretty good right?

839
01:33:09.291 --> 01:33:11.519
First I stole paralytic
from infirmary then I

840
01:33:11.544 --> 01:33:13.916
shot her up when she was
freaking out about you.

841
01:33:13.961 --> 01:33:15.938
I mean I told these guys
I was pretty smart.

842
01:33:15.963 --> 01:33:17.413
I guess they should've listened.

843
01:33:23.580 --> 01:33:27.271
- You're real!
- Yeah I'm real.

844
01:33:29.370 --> 01:33:34.289
- What are you doing here?
- You die. I die.

845
01:33:37.943 --> 01:33:40.772
Ohh... okay guys come on.
Lets go. seriously.

846
01:33:40.797 --> 01:33:42.211
You can do that later.

847
01:33:43.152 --> 01:33:44.628
- You're ok?
- Yeah.

848
01:33:48.782 --> 01:33:51.563
- Thank you. Peter.
- Yeah whatever. No we're even. stiff.

849
01:33:52.270 --> 01:33:53.365
Alright. come on let's go.

850
01:33:53.565 --> 01:33:55.915
- Before Jeanine realizes we're gone.
-

851
01:33:56.690 --> 01:33:58.794
- What?
- The box! We have to get the box!

852
01:33:58.795 --> 01:34:00.927
Are you kidding me?
Now is not the time for souvenir tris!

853
01:34:00.928 --> 01:34:02.326
Four. you have to listen to me.

854
01:34:02.565 --> 01:34:04.365
It's not what Jeanine think
it is. I know it's not.

855
01:34:04.390 --> 01:34:05.710
My mother would
have destroyed it.

856
01:34:06.559 --> 01:34:08.125
We have to get it.

857
01:34:11.583 --> 01:34:14.013
Peter. is there another way to the lab?

858
01:34:14.706 --> 01:34:17.664
I mean. I have to go to the control
room to disable all the doors.

859
01:34:17.665 --> 01:34:19.092
Okay you do that!

860
01:34:21.272 --> 01:34:22.823
- Okay. right now?
- Yeah.

861
01:34:23.084 --> 01:34:25.355
You just choose our side
whether you meant to or not.

862
01:34:25.665 --> 01:34:27.935
If you want to survive. make sure we do.

863
01:34:29.100 --> 01:34:30.140
Let's go!

864
01:34:33.068 --> 01:34:34.068
Fuck!

865
01:35:02.849 --> 01:35:05.350
No guns. It draws less attention.

866
01:35:07.381 --> 01:35:09.429
- Hey.
- Hold up!

867
01:35:20.201 --> 01:35:21.783
- Access Denied.
- Come on!

868
01:35:49.446 --> 01:35:51.681
- Access granted.
- Let's go..

869
01:35:54.091 --> 01:35:55.729
- Is that it?
- Yes.

870
01:35:55.818 --> 01:35:57.470
Grab it and let's go.

871
01:36:00.789 --> 01:36:04.772
- Security breach.
- What's going on?

872
01:36:07.510 --> 01:36:09.818
- What's going on? What is it?
- There's been a breach in the sim room.

873
01:36:09.819 --> 01:36:11.965
I want to see who the hell is in there.

874
01:36:11.966 --> 01:36:13.957
- The cameras are down in that sector.
- I'll send the guards there.

875
01:36:13.958 --> 01:36:16.856
Bring up every cell!

876
01:36:16.858 --> 01:36:18.000
Now!

877
01:36:25.007 --> 01:36:26.106
Show her.

878
01:36:26.958 --> 01:36:29.071
Tori finally found a way
to get them out safely.

879
01:36:29.072 --> 01:36:32.373
- How many others?
- Every last one of them.

880
01:36:36.390 --> 01:36:37.467
Let's go!

881
01:36:41.293 --> 01:36:44.531
Tris! Tris. come on. we gotta move.

882
01:36:45.915 --> 01:36:47.357
Tris we have to move!

883
01:36:48.217 --> 01:36:50.955
I can't!. I can't.

884
01:36:51.243 --> 01:36:52.410
My mom died protecting

885
01:36:52.435 --> 01:36:53.813
what ever is inside this.

886
01:36:55.634 --> 01:36:56.863
I have to open it for her

887
01:36:56.888 --> 01:36:58.042
and I think I know how.

888
01:36:58.043 --> 01:37:01.516
- If we dont leave here now we're not getting out.
- I have to do this first.

889
01:37:02.110 --> 01:37:04.829
I know it doesn't make much sense
but you have to trust me. please.

890
01:37:06.814 --> 01:37:08.609
You have my life apparently.

891
01:37:14.992 --> 01:37:16.407
Get in.

892
01:37:21.164 --> 01:37:22.239
Don't move!

893
01:37:27.833 --> 01:37:29.610
Initializing Amity sim.

894
01:37:34.059 --> 01:37:35.766
Back again are we.

895
01:37:37.058 --> 01:37:39.454
You're an even bigger
fool than your mother.

896
01:37:44.199 --> 01:37:46.481
You can say whatever you want Jeanine.

897
01:37:47.606 --> 01:37:49.321
But I'm not gonna fight you.

898
01:37:50.158 --> 01:37:52.832
- How very Amity of you.
- I mean it.

899
01:37:55.018 --> 01:37:58.054
- I'm not gonna fight you.
- Of course you're not.

900
01:37:59.052 --> 01:38:01.253
You're gonna fight her.

901
01:38:04.047 --> 01:38:05.905
The one you really hate.

902
01:38:38.617 --> 01:38:39.887
What are you?

903
01:38:42.820 --> 01:38:44.862
I'm you. Tris.

904
01:38:46.087 --> 01:38:48.283
I'm the real you.

905
01:38:58.648 --> 01:38:59.821
I'm not gonna fight you.

906
01:39:00.274 --> 01:39:02.258
- I'll make you fight me.
- You're not me.

907
01:39:02.259 --> 01:39:05.696
I am. I'm what the others see
when they're looking at you.

908
01:39:21.730 --> 01:39:25.392
You killed Will and your parents.
You're deadly.

909
01:39:26.177 --> 01:39:27.293
Enough!

910
01:39:31.602 --> 01:39:35.565
No one's gonna love you Tris.
They're not even gonna miss you.

911
01:39:35.566 --> 01:39:37.823
This world will only be
better off without you.

912
01:39:38.023 --> 01:39:40.666
One less Divergent ruining things.

913
01:39:40.776 --> 01:39:46.866
And no one will ever forgive
you for what you've done.

914
01:39:47.751 --> 01:39:49.065
You're wrong.

915
01:39:57.038 --> 01:40:00.310
Because I will.

916
01:40:37.110 --> 01:40:39.497
Amity sim complete.

917
01:40:43.053 --> 01:40:44.711
- No!
- No! Stop!

918
01:40:49.071 --> 01:40:51.664
Initializing message.

919
01:41:10.468 --> 01:41:11.659
Hello.

920
01:41:12.230 --> 01:41:14.072
I come from outside the wall.

921
01:41:14.842 --> 01:41:17.447
Where we have all destroyed each other.

922
01:41:17.965 --> 01:41:21.777
We designed your city as an experiment.

923
01:41:22.403 --> 01:41:26.537
We believed it was the only way to recover
the humanity we had lost.

924
01:41:29.170 --> 01:41:32.299
And we created factions to ensure peace.

925
01:41:33.672 --> 01:41:38.322
We believed that there will be those among
you who will transcend these factions.

926
01:41:39.745 --> 01:41:42.054
These will be the Divergent.

927
01:41:43.996 --> 01:41:46.551
They are the true purpose
of the experiment.

928
01:41:46.552 --> 01:41:51.222
They are vital to humanity's survival.

929
01:41:52.767 --> 01:41:58.062
If you're watching this now than at least one of
you are proof that our experiment has succeeded.

930
01:41:59.603 --> 01:42:05.760
The time has come for you to emerge
from your isolation and rejoin us.

931
01:42:05.879 --> 01:42:09.260
We have allowed you to believe
that you're the last of us.

932
01:42:09.261 --> 01:42:11.052
but you're not.

933
01:42:11.634 --> 01:42:16.399
Mankind waits for you. with hope.

934
01:42:16.599 --> 01:42:18.928
beyond the wall.

935
01:42:26.371 --> 01:42:28.896
- You're okay?
- Yeah.

936
01:42:32.667 --> 01:42:33.768
Yes.

937
01:42:51.323 --> 01:42:53.827
You're wrong about us.

938
01:42:57.668 --> 01:43:02.933
We were never the problem.
We're the solution.

939
01:43:15.202 --> 01:43:17.783
- Bury the box.
- What?

940
01:43:17.784 --> 01:43:20.609
No one sees it. Ever.

941
01:43:24.174 --> 01:43:25.624
Kill them both.

942
01:43:25.682 --> 01:43:26.820
No!

943
01:43:33.990 --> 01:43:35.151
Don't move.

944
01:43:39.745 --> 01:43:42.247
Put your weapons down now!

945
01:43:42.248 --> 01:43:46.712
- Stay!
- Do not move!

946
01:43:50.538 --> 01:43:51.985
Hello. Jeanine.

947
01:43:53.607 --> 01:43:54.831
Evelyn.

948
01:43:54.832 --> 01:43:56.711
Impressive.

949
01:43:56.871 --> 01:43:58.680
I think we're gonna like it here.

950
01:43:59.563 --> 01:44:02.476
Do you honestly think the other
factions will stand for this?

951
01:44:03.057 --> 01:44:05.068
Because you're so popular?

952
01:44:07.511 --> 01:44:09.062
Get her out of here.

953
01:44:09.853 --> 01:44:11.815
When that message gets

954
01:44:11.840 --> 01:44:13.979
out it will be the end.

955
01:44:31.663 --> 01:44:33.385
What message?

956
01:44:36.938 --> 01:44:39.094
You'll see. I'm gonna put it

957
01:44:39.119 --> 01:44:41.427
on every monitor in the city.

958
01:44:43.773 --> 01:44:46.446
We have seperated you from the rest of us.

959
01:44:48.418 --> 01:44:51.673
And we created factions to ensure peace.

960
01:44:53.568 --> 01:44:58.169
The time has come for you to emerge
from your isolation and rejoin us.

961
01:44:59.515 --> 01:45:03.073
We have allowed you to believe
that you're the last of us.

962
01:45:03.252 --> 01:45:04.501
but you're not.

963
01:45:05.077 --> 01:45:11.296
If you're watching this now than at least one of
you are proof that our experiment has succeeded.

964
01:45:14.192 --> 01:45:18.334
Mankind waits for you. with hope.

965
01:45:19.161 --> 01:45:22.214
beyond the wall.

966
01:45:58.406 --> 01:46:00.040
These will be the Divergent.

967
01:46:00.041 --> 01:46:02.684
They are the true purpose
of the experiment.

968
01:46:02.685 --> 01:46:06.247
They are vital to humanity's survival.

969
01:46:06.540 --> 01:46:07.881
You did it.

970
01:46:16.419 --> 01:46:18.720
Everyone's staring at me.

971
01:46:19.492 --> 01:46:21.304
You changed everything.

972
01:46:23.460 --> 01:46:24.859
What now?

973
01:46:25.991 --> 01:46:27.763
Only one way to find out.

974
01:46:28.901 --> 01:46:29.902
Are you ready?

975
01:47:34.660 --> 01:47:36.836
It's been over 200 years.

976
01:47:39.964 --> 01:47:41.570
Who knows what's out there?

977
01:47:44.412 --> 01:47:46.110
You'll never find out.
